+## Untested scope
+- `OrdinaryIdentity::continuity` intake with a keyed claim (`src/identity/repair.rs:452`): no test sends a keyed `ContinuityCheckIn` through it, so a regression to `Cooperative` at that call site would pass every test found, including `a_claim_rests_on_its_key_when_it_presents_one`.
+- `reconcile_published_page_for` with a `RetiredReversibly` outcome (`src/identity/reconcile.rs:572`): `tests/identity/reconcile.rs` has no case asserting that a reversible close counts in `transition_count` and not in `retirements_started`; `tests/store/restored_pane.rs:594` applies transitions below this function.
+- `reconcile_invalidated_page` refusing `RetiredReversibly` (`src/identity/reconcile.rs:644`): no test reaches this defensive arm, and its message `host invalidation cannot retire a seat` appears nowhere in `tests/`.
+
+## Deferred OK
+- Narrow the doc comment on `a_claim_rests_on_its_key_when_it_presents_one` (`tests/identity/kept_continuity_rules.rs:72`), which claims to kill call-site regressions that it does not; the helper's own behaviour is what it pins.
